(3. Leave) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.1 Annual leave) Tj T*
(Full-time employees receive 20 days of paid annual leave per calendar year. Leave accrues) Tj T*
(monthly at 1.67 days per month. Up to 5 unused days may be carried over to the next year;) Tj T*
(anything above 5 days lapses on 31 December. Annual leave requests of 3 or more) Tj T*
(consecutive days must be submitted at least 2 weeks in advance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.2 Casual leave) Tj T*
(Employees receive 8 days of casual leave per year for short, unplanned absences. Casual) Tj T*
(leave cannot be carried over and cannot be combined with annual leave to extend a holiday.) Tj T*
(No more than 2 consecutive days of casual leave may be taken at once.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.3 Sick leave) Tj T*
(Employees receive 10 days of paid sick leave per year. A medical certificate is required) Tj T*
(for sick leave of 3 or more consecutive days. Unused sick leave does not carry over.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.4 Parental leave) Tj T*
(Birthing parents receive 26 weeks of paid maternity leave. Non-birthing parents receive 4) Tj T*
(weeks of paid paternity leave, which must be taken within 6 months of the child's birth or) Tj T*
(adoption. Adoptive parents receive the same leave as birthing parents if the child is) Tj T*
(under 3 months old.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.5 Public holidays) Tj T*
(Acme observes 12 public holidays per year. The list is published by People Operations) Tj T*
(every December for the following year.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 280 30 Td (Page 2 of 4) Tj ET
